      "dcterms:format": "application/json",
      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"document material discrepancies by submission of one or more of the listed documents\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[\"(1) Court orders or decrees:\\n\\n(a) Name change orders; or\\n\\n(b) Divorce decrees;\",\"(2) Certificates of naturalization;\",\"(3) Marriage certificates;\",\"(4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or\",\"(5) Documentation of customary usage.\"],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:d0710ebb01c25d1821ac0056d465cd80ea46bb1fd6dde5ebc4b87a41f0745baa\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:66f8d8bf444aac8e4759b6f8baa27cdca56f92a5fb99e7bb80d9df1028eb208d\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:2fd60277f8e1a0e757565c42488e517e2ecba4ecec615cab209f129daf61dbfe\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:a6f133fbaa6443f4b1053d4446ad75272bcaae0d7dbdd2161b747947ef05a573\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:2b20ac8d563d612eb87786abdbb2c6e49c0c58b1aa3119f34d426cafe9ce34bd\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:6d2a778f5a785c4a17ee0c818ae0502cb31a9b0ea50a14b31d22f4e9272dc89d\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:729a3da6c2cfcab188dc9cec2d1f38f684ff250bed1419e13897cff127dcfc9e\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:51ae8df9f907cf92304caa1121e31da02ae2c30a51f1a323c7c885198a81b778\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:57036a293a1df97ec4f1b6cd9ad14b4e8530a88f27acccf120f5491d72ef8a66\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:f645ccc793c8eb0647632b9b33ccfa8449e52add223d0d5c6bc0a7df79d123d7\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:8cfd599b74633d485444605dc119102bb2b76ca51ce421ecb9d66f997c829ffc\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:189c49ccad116d17cbcc63213c1894425ff9b8c8c061408ba259d4ba8137b526\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:5524c160516adcb29da29e1075d80d9d4adba99a1c4fddbae4de3d3f50977128\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:45f7ae0677d3d2fc0dc3103b81d99cb45107717a9b4fdfaf114df37708ea6e41\"],\"choice_quote\":\"submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C)). Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\\n\\n(1) Court orders or decrees:\\n\\n(a) Name change orders; or\\n\\n(b) Divorce decrees;\\n\\n(2) Certificates of naturalization;\\n\\n(3) Marriage certificates;\\n\\n(4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or\\n\\n(5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\"choice_text\":\"One or more of: (1) Court orders or decrees: (a) Name change orders, or (b) Divorce decrees; (2) Certificates of naturalization; (3) Marriage certificates; (4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or (5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\"claimants\":[{\"attribution\":\"rkaf:claimantIsDocumentIssuer\",\"quote\":\"8 FAM 403.1-4\",\"text\":\"Department of State\"}],\"concepts\":[{\"definition\":\"Requirement to document material name discrepancies by submitting one or more acceptable documents.\",\"label\":\"Documenting Material Name Changes\",\"quote\":\"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C)).\",\"role\":\"rkaf:assignmentPrimary\"}],\"context_quotes\":[],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":1075,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":1075,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:413:1075:sha256-660d269ce0e0ee226093dd3c78c292d98b7ef7de1af61f8431adecf82778afc6\",\"quote\":\"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C)). Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\\n\\n(1) Court orders or decrees:\\n\\n(a) Name change orders; or\\n\\n(b) Divorce decrees;\\n\\n(2) Certificates of naturalization;\\n\\n(3) Marriage certificates;\\n\\n(4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or\\n\\n(5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\"start\":413},{\"end\":672,\"field\":\"action\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:585:672:sha256-3f80573ab687cf40cee9c879860f5c4983790d85bd533ae805d1a2225f683376\",\"quote\":\"must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section\",\"start\":585},{\"end\":584,\"field\":\"object\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:413:584:sha256-cb40404d70d90218b38e38b5d38aea0168c012097c2d557a928d6edea4eed5fa\",\"quote\":\"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity\",\"start\":413},{\"end\":589,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:585:589:sha256-4137b01e139589b7a1d3b3fc4da031d8ce5bb415808734e970c3a58ea0e98f0f\",\"quote\":\"must\",\"start\":585},{\"end\":1075,\"field\":\"choice_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:607:1075:sha256-890f312205d2261634b9a6bb749f395e54a561047998f9e88782f6a048402f8a\",\"quote\":\"submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C)). Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\\n\\n(1) Court orders or decrees:\\n\\n(a) Name change orders; or\\n\\n(b) Divorce decrees;\\n\\n(2) Certificates of naturalization;\\n\\n(3) Marriage certificates;\\n\\n(4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or\\n\\n(5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\"start\":607},{\"end\":729,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:673:729:sha256-3a7a124d5b8dc929b2aab1d9a0c18ace4e99057a8a55f81f159abefae7fd9a2e\",\"quote\":\"(see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C))\",\"start\":673},{\"end\":893,\"field\":\"alternative:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:815:893:sha256-d6390302a88f9630b4f53601fa944885da49039388f4323bdc1e3c1c88f860b7\",\"quote\":\"(1) Court orders or decrees:\\n\\n(a) Name change orders; or\\n\\n(b) Divorce decrees;\",\"start\":815},{\"end\":930,\"field\":\"alternative:1\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:895:930:sha256-4e18e0787882e8309ae3622b09e55a5651877e9c53a350497910971ae7b678c2\",\"quote\":\"(2) Certificates of naturalization;\",\"start\":895},{\"end\":958,\"field\":\"alternative:2\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:932:958:sha256-e5cd8687a08df7afb024ac63f03ef7d3f67ae346933e9b1efe14a78515b76ad3\",\"quote\":\"(3) Marriage certificates;\",\"start\":932},{\"end\":1036,\"field\":\"alternative:3\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:960:1036:sha256-ae2aa14b1493569032e9e081d8f62feacfbdd7a24ce612d931ecbbeebb32c0f2\",\"quote\":\"(4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or\",\"start\":960},{\"end\":1075,\"field\":\"alternative:4\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:1038:1075:sha256-94a68417342a7382810a40ae0bcea207f5efacf3def75383c8abe1a81fc0d9bc\",\"quote\":\"(5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\"start\":1038},{\"end\":730,\"field\":\"concepts:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:413:730:sha256-f5c50ee630319381829f3f686765da81dc46b5e12ebd9229ccadc6ef099e2723\",\"quote\":\"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C)).\",\"start\":413},{\"end\":725,\"field\":\"claimants:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:712:725:sha256-a96c20412c405134c053a23dcad1eed527e8d972a8b45b6697d3384b89ee6c33\",\"quote\":\"8 FAM 403.1-4\",\"start\":712}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:5ac1c734a39ff7bf12ec3bed1747fefb20f949059bae6d03abb9009db02f30f7\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"one or more of the documents listed in this section ... (1) Court orders or decrees: (a) Name change orders; or (b) Divorce decrees; (2) Certificates of naturalization; (3) Marriage certificates; (4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or (5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:5524c160516adcb29da29e1075d80d9d4adba99a1c4fddbae4de3d3f50977128\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"must\",\"object\":\"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:83574b361a01e4c011dc89a22e8cf11552e0ab3faa424ede20ca98e139499889\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the applicant's evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submission of one or more of the documents listed in this section (see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C)). Acceptable means of documenting a material name change include (per 22 CFR 51.25):\\n\\n(1) Court orders or decrees:\\n\\n(a) Name change orders; or\\n\\n(b) Divorce decrees;\\n\\n(2) Certificates of naturalization;\\n\\n(3) Marriage certificates;\\n\\n(4) Documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law; or\\n\\n(5) Documentation of customary usage.\",\"references\":[\"8 FAM 403.1-4(C)\",\"22 CFR 51.25\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:02a90cb682c4e90922cdec2b6cfcc48594010af3853171579022cbc795380b8a\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(see an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C))\"],\"scope_text\":\"Except for married names as provided in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C).\",\"section_id\":\"fam-names-section-4\",\"start\":413,\"summary\":\"Material discrepancies between the name recorded on the application, the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality, or the evidence of identity must be documented by submitting one or more of the listed acceptable documents (court orders/decrees including name change orders or divorce decrees, certificates of naturalization, marriage certificates, documentation demonstrating change of name by operation of state law, or documentation of customary usage), subject to an exception for married names in 8 FAM 403.1-4(C).\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
